From: Onigiri
Subject: [PATCH] Keep Camera controls upright with the cover upside down

On a display that is landscape by default, Camera turns its whole layout
180 degrees when the display is at 180, keeping the controls fixed to the
hardware. On the cover that put the shutter at the top when the phone is held
hinge down. Lay it out as at 0 instead, as Camera already does on portrait
displays. The preview is a SurfaceView, which stays upright on its own.

diff --git a/smali_classes3/com/sec/android/app/camera/MainLayout.smali b/smali_classes3/com/sec/android/app/camera/MainLayout.smali
--- a/smali_classes3/com/sec/android/app/camera/MainLayout.smali
+++ b/smali_classes3/com/sec/android/app/camera/MainLayout.smali
@@ -375,7 +375,8 @@
     goto :goto_1

     :cond_6
-    const/16 v0, 0xb4
+    # Onigiri: hinge down on the cover is rotation 180; keep the shutter at the bottom.
+    move v0, v5

     :goto_1
     iput v0, p0, Lcom/sec/android/app/camera/MainLayout;->mRotation:I
